<title>JAPAN: Japan utility puts out minor fire at nuclear plant.</title>
<headline>Japan utility puts out minor fire at nuclear plant.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc (TEPCO), Japan's largest power utility, said on Friday it had extinguished a small fire which broke out in the building housing a nuclear reactor in Fukushima, northern Japan.</p>
<p>The fire, which broke out at about 1423 JST, was put out in seven minutes. The incident has not affected operation of TEPCO's Fukushima No.2 reactor, with a capacity of 1.1 million kilowatts, nor contaminated the surrounding environment, TEPCO said. No one was injured.</p>
</text>
